.TH MDD.PFID_UPDATE_ATTEMPTS 4 2026-11-06 Lustre "Lustre Kernel Interfaces"
.SH NAME
mdd.pfid_update_attempts \- PFID update counters
.SH SYNOPSIS
.SY
.BI "lctl get_param mdd." MDT_NAME .pfid_update_attempts
.SY
.BI "lctl get_param mdd." MDT_NAME .pfid_update_failures
.SY
.BI "lctl get_param mdd." MDT_NAME .pfid_update_enospc
.YS
.SS PROPERTIES
.TP
.B Access Permissions
.br
.BR 444 " | " -r--r--r--
.TP
.B Scope
.br
Per-MDT device.
.TP
.B Config
.br
Always present for MDT devices.
.SH DESCRIPTION
After a layout merge, split, or swap, the MDT attempts to update the parent
FID (PFID) and component information stored in the affected OST objects.
These counters report PFID replacement attempts per file, rather than the
number of OST objects or objects awaiting repair.
The counters are reset to zero when the MDT is mounted.
.TP
.B pfid_update_attempts
Number of PFID replacement attempts, including failures to create a transaction.
.TP
.B pfid_update_failures
Number of attempts that returned an error, including transaction-stop errors.
.TP
.B pfid_update_enospc
Number of failed attempts that returned ENOSPC.
.PP
A PFID update failure does not undo the preceding layout operation or report
that completed operation as failed to the client.
The counters do not indicate whether a later operation or layout LFSCK repaired
the affected objects.
.SH EXAMPLES
Read the counters for all MDTs mounted on this server:
.EX
.RB "mds# " "lctl get_param 'mdd.*.pfid_update_*'"
.EE
.SH AVAILABILITY
.B pfid_update_attempts
is part of the
.BR lustre (7)
filesystem package since release 2.18.0.
.\" Added in commit 2.17.61-1 (LU-21122).
